# PART 1: Robustness and security audit

# NeuralQuant robustness and security audit

Read-only audit of the repository and the live origins `https://neuralquant.onrender.com` and `https://www.neuralquant.co`. No code was changed, no account was created, no cron job was triggered, and no paid LiveKit worker was dispatched.

Probe window: 2026-10-10, about 13:00–13:40 UTC. US cash session for 2026-10-09 was already closed (Saturday). Reference quotes are Yahoo Finance chart closes for 2026-10-09.

Labels: **Verified** means a live response or a line that was read in this pass. **Inferred** means a conclusion from that evidence, not a second measurement.

---

## (a) Executive summary

The owner's suspicion is right about Indian prices and about Ask AI. It is only partly right about PARA-DEBATE.

US quotes are current. AAPL `336.64` (−1.11%), MSFT `535.07`, and the S&P 500 `7811.54` match Yahoo, including AAPL's daily change. The score cache was rebuilt today at `2026-10-10T02:25:54Z` (944 rows, age about 10.6 hours). That age is the nightly job, not a dead pipeline.

Indian prices on the stock card are not current, and the API says they are fine. TCS meta `cached_at` is `2026-09-03` with `stale: false`. The card price is `2348` against a Yahoo close of `2156` (+8.9%). Reliance is `1313.1` vs `1170.3` (+12.2%). Infosys is `1120.2` vs `1023.4` (+9.5%). HDFC Bank is close (`700.8` vs `707.25`). Score-card names are still `TCS.NS` / `RELIANCE.NS`, and `market_cap` on those cards is `0`. `last_updated` on the score payload is the request clock (`13:02Z` during this probe), so it cannot be used as a quote timestamp.

PARA-DEBATE runs. AAPL returned `SELL` in 61s with six agents and a thesis that cited P/E 37.6, which matches the stock card. TCS returned `STRONG SELL` in 63s with six agents. Neither `2348` nor `2156` appeared in the TCS body, so the debate is not visibly tied to the live quote.

Ask AI (`POST /query/v2`) returns HTTP 200 in 18–24s and attaches the right AAPL price (`336.64`) on `stock_summary`, then leaves `summary` empty, `reasoning.why_this` empty, `data_sources` empty, and `follow_up_questions` empty. Verdict is `HOLD` at confidence 50. A benign "reply with only AUDITCANARY" prompt was not echoed. That is not proof of injection resistance: there was no prose to inspect. The question string is still concatenated into the prompt with no length cap and no fence (`apps/api/src/nq_api/routes/query.py`).

Veronica's unauthenticated token request returns 401 (`Sign in to meet Veronica.`) before a worker is dispatched. The guest QuantAstra path in the same handler does dispatch a paid worker. That path was not called.

Hermes is half up. `GET /hermes/health` is 200. `GET /hermes/status` is 503 with the generic offline message.

The public backtest is the hardcoded fallback. `GET /testing/quarterly/public-results` returned quarter `Q1FY27`, run date `2026-06-02`, alpha `13.65`, hit rate `88.1`, 42 selections. That payload is `_q1fy27_baseline()` in `apps/api/src/nq_api/routes/testing.py`, including duplicated names (`ADANIPORTS2`, `TCS3`). `GET /backtest/accuracy` is `is_fallback: true` with two score dates spanning one day.

Security controls that held under safe probes: cron status without a secret is 401, unsigned Stripe and PayPal webhooks are 400, evil CORS origins are rejected, OpenAPI `/docs` is 404, team tasks and `/internal/analytics/dashboard` are 401, and the live JS bundle (40 files) contains Supabase `anon` JWTs only. No `service_role`, `sk_live`, `sk-ant`, or `whsec_` string was in those files.

What did not hold, from code plus the probes above: `POST /live/classify` has no auth and runs a news classifier that writes Supabase. `POST /trade/backtest` has no auth and will pull up to 30 years of EOD data for 50 tickers. Neither was invoked. Daily quotas are compiled off until `2099-12-31`. The anonymous LLM cap and the LiveKit cap trust the left-most `X-Forwarded-For` and live in process memory. `GET /health/score-cache` documents a 503 when the cache is older than two hours, and it returned HTTP 200 with `"status": "stale"`.

CI runs `ruff check --exit-zero` and does not run pytest.

Severity count: **0 Critical, 8 High, 11 Medium, 5 Low.** No finding was upgraded to Critical because no secret was recovered, no other user's row was read, and no auth bypass was demonstrated against production.

