## 6. How the patent fits, and the decisions before 7 July 2027

### 6.1 What the patent is for

- **What you have.** Indian provisional 202631083313, filed 7 July 2026 (number format suggests the Kolkata office), with you as sole applicant and inventor. The title leads with "regime-adaptive multi-factor equity research signals using a multi-agent adversarial debate framework". Your own description says it "leads on" the verification gate [EXT §2].
- **Its realistic role** **[INFERENCE]**:
  - credibility with licensees
  - a modest deterrent
  - an asset that raises sale value (Direction F)

  It is not a moat on its own. Your own prior-art search rated its strength 2 out of 5 [EXT §2]. Debate-based claims face close prior art in TradingAgents, FinDebate and AlphaAgents [EXT §2.2]. Indian s3(k) excludes business methods and computer programs "per se" [EXT §2.2].
- **The strongest framing.** Deterministic interception and correction of LLM numeric outputs against provenance-tagged data, with an audit log. That is a technical effect (output reliability in a computing system), which is the kind of framing the 2025 CRI Guidelines allow (https://ipindia.gov.in/frontend/pdf/patents/guidelines/GUIDELINES%20FOR%20EXAMINATION%20OF%20COMPUTER%20RELATED%20INVENTIONS%20%28CRIs%29%20-%202025.pdf) [EXT §2.2]. It is also exactly what Verify sells. **The product and the patent now point the same way.**
- **A truthfulness point.** The provisional specification describes a correction log and three reliability classes, and presents worked examples as "observed in a production implementation". The code logs similar corrections, but it doesn't implement the log or the classes [CODE §2.5, §4.3]. Building M3 and M5 before filing the complete specification closes that gap, so the specification describes a system that actually exists.

